\text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \times (b_1 + b_2) \times h
\] where \(b_1\) and \(b_2\) are the lengths of the two parallel sides, and \(h\) is the height. In this case, the two parallel sides are AB and CD, and the height is the perpendicular distance between them. The length of AB is 2 units (from 0 to -2 on the y-axis), and the length of CD is 6 units (from 0 to 6 on the y-axis). The height is the distance between the x-coordinates of A and C, which is 4 units. Plugging these values into the formula, we get: \[
